{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X8GdYct4DtvB8sfwU4NES4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd091-chown\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/chown: Change File Owner and Group\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  macOS ships a BSD chown that differs from GNU chown in recursive traversal flags,\n6\t  symlink handling, and OWNER:GROUP parsing. The Go implementation must match the\n7\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchown, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n8\t  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Change the owner and/or group of files using OWNER, OWNER:GROUP, OWNER:, :GROUP, or numeric UID:GID syntax.\n12\t  - G2: Support recursive ownership changes with -R and symlink traversal control.\n13\t  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchown via differential testing.\n14\t\n15\trequirements:\n16\t  R1:\n17\t    title: Ownership specification\n18\t    items:\n19\t      - R1.1:\n20\t          text: \"Must accept OWNER[:GROUP] syntax: OWNER changes only owner, OWNER:GROUP changes both, OWNER: changes owner and sets group to OWNER's login group, :GROUP changes only group.\"\n21\t      - R1.2:\n22\t          text: OWNER and GROUP may be names or numeric IDs. Must resolve names to IDs via the system user/group database.\n23\t      - R1.3:\n24\t          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's owner and group to match RFILE's.\"\n25\t      - R1.4:\n26\t          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the owner/group is invalid, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n27\t\n28\t  R2:\n29\t    title: Recursive and symlink handling\n30\t    items:\n31\t      - R2.1:\n32\t          text: \"-R or --recursive must change ownership recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n33\t      - R2.2:\n34\t          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must change the symlink itself rather than the target.\"\n35\t      - R2.3:\n36\t          text: \"-H must follow symlinks on the command line only. -L must follow all symlinks. -P must never follow symlinks (default with -R).\"\n37\t\n38\t  R3:\n39\t    title: Output control and exit codes\n40\t    items:\n41\t      - R3.1:\n42\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed. -c or --changes must print only when changes are made. -f or --silent must suppress most errors.\"\n43\t      - R3.2:\n44\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n45\t      - R3.3:\n46\t          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n47\t\n48\tnon_goals:\n49\t  - cmd/chown does not implement --preserve-root.\n50\t  - cmd/chown does not implement --from=CURRENT_OWNER:CURRENT_GROUP conditional change.\n51\t\n52\tacceptance_criteria:\n53\t  - id: AC1\n54\t    criterion: \"chown user:staff file changes owner and group, matching gchown.\"\n55\t    traces:\n56\t      - R1.1\n57\t      - R1.2\n58\t  - id: AC2\n59\t    criterion: \"chown -R user dir recursively changes owner, matching gchown -R.\"\n60\t    traces:\n61\t      - R2.1\n62\t  - id: AC3\n63\t    criterion: \"chown :staff file changes only group, matching gchown.\"\n64\t    traces:\n65\t      - R1.1\n66\t  - id: AC4\n67\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gchown passes for all required test cases.\"\n68\t    traces:\n69\t      - R1.1\n70\t      - R1.2\n71\t      - R2.1\n72\t  - id: AC5\n73\t    criterion: \"cmd/chown compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n74\t    traces:\n75\t      - R1.1\n76\t      - R1.2\n77\t      - R1.3\n78\t      - R1.4\n79\t      - R2.1\n80\t      - R2.2\n81\t      - R2.3\n82\t      - R3.1\n83\t      - R3.2\n84\t      - R3.3\n85\t\n86\tpackage_contract:\n87\t  imports:\n88\t    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n89\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a39bb1de-8019-4cee-97a2-987b3a588d8f","uuid":"799ac4a7-7093-4562-a10e-b9cfdb9bf2da","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:55:09.240Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd091-chown.yaml","content":"id: srd091-chown\ntitle: \"cmd/chown: Change File Owner and Group\"\n\nproblem: |\n  macOS ships a BSD chown that differs from GNU chown in recursive traversal flags,\n  symlink handling, and OWNER:GROUP parsing. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gchown, installed by coreutils) byte-for-byte on all\n  flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Change the owner and/or group of files using OWNER, OWNER:GROUP, OWNER:, :GROUP, or numeric UID:GID syntax.\n  - G2: Support recursive ownership changes with -R and symlink traversal control.\n  - G3: Verify functional parity against gchown via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Ownership specification\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"Must accept OWNER[:GROUP] syntax: OWNER changes only owner, OWNER:GROUP changes both, OWNER: changes owner and sets group to OWNER's login group, :GROUP changes only group.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: OWNER and GROUP may be names or numeric IDs. Must resolve names to IDs via the system user/group database.\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"--reference=RFILE must set each FILE's owner and group to match RFILE's.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any file cannot be accessed or the owner/group is invalid, printing an error to stderr, and continue processing remaining files.\n\n  R2:\n    title: Recursive and symlink handling\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-R or --recursive must change ownership recursively for directories and their contents.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-h or --no-dereference must change the symlink itself rather than the target.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-H must follow symlinks on the command line only. -L must follow all symlinks. -P must never follow symlinks (default with -R).\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Output control and exit codes\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print a diagnostic for every file processed. -c or --changes must print only when changes are made. -f or --silent must suppress most errors.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are processed successfully. Must exit 1 on any error.\n      - R3.3:\n          text: Must handle SIGPIPE gracefully (exit 0) using pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler.\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/chown does not implement --preserve-root.\n  - cmd/chown does not implement --from=CURRENT_OWNER:CURRENT_GROUP conditional change.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"chown user:staff file changes owner and group, matching gchown.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"chown -R user dir recursively changes owner, matching gchown -R.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"chown :staff file changes only group, matching gchown.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gchown passes for all required test cases.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"cmd/chown compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n\npackage_contract:\n  imports:\n    - github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\n","numLines":89,"startLine":1,"totalLines":89}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01ETGimS82QXtx5cUUAsjyEv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YCGRVcHBW7gsfQXkwpqquc","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/cmd/chown/main.go"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":200177,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":200177},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a39bb1de-8019-4cee-97a2-987b3a588d8f","uuid":"50fbdafa-e68a-4c9a-98f3-6beefef376d3"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YCGRVcHBW7gsfQXkwpqquc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n3\t\n4\t// cmd/chown implements srd091-chown R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3.\n5\tpackage main\n6\t\n7\timport (\n8\t\t\"errors\"\n9\t\t\"fmt\"\n10\t\t\"os\"\n11\t\t\"os/user\"\n12\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n13\t\t\"strconv\"\n14\t\t\"strings\"\n15\t\n16\t\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n17\t)\n18\t\n19\tconst helpText = `Usage: chown [OPTION]... [OWNER][:[GROUP]] FILE...\n20\t  or:  chown [OPTION]... --reference=RFILE FILE...\n21\tChange the owner and/or group of each FILE to OWNER and/or GROUP.\n22\t\n23\t  -c, --changes          like verbose but report only when a change is made\n24\t  -f, --silent, --quiet  suppress most error messages\n25\t  -v, --verbose          output a diagnostic for every file processed\n26\t      --dereference      affect the referent of each symbolic link (this is\n27\t                         the default), rather than the symbolic link itself\n28\t  -h, --no-dereference   affect symbolic links instead of any referenced file\n29\t      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially (the default)\n30\t      --preserve-root    fail to operate recursively on '/'\n31\t      --reference=RFILE  use RFILE's owner and group rather than specifying\n32\t                         OWNER:GROUP values\n33\t  -R, --recursive        operate on files and directories recursively\n34\t  -H                     if a command line argument is a symbolic link\n35\t                         to a directory, traverse it\n36\t  -L                     traverse every symbolic link to a directory\n37\t                         encountered\n38\t  -P                     do not traverse any symbolic links (default)\n39\t      --help     display this help and exit\n40\t      --version  output version information and exit\n41\t\n42\tOwner is unchanged if missing.  Group is unchanged if missing, but changed\n43\tto login group if implied by a ':' following a symbolic OWNER.\n44\tOWNER and GROUP may be numeric as well as symbolic.\n45\t\n46\tExamples:\n47\t  chown root /u        Change the owner of /u to \"root\".\n48\t  chown root:staff /u  Change the owner of /u to \"root\" and the\n49\t                       group to \"staff\".\n50\t  chown -hR root /u    Change the owner of /u and subfiles to \"root\".\n51\t`\n52\t\n53\tconst versionText = `chown (go-unix-utils) dev\n54\t`\n55\t\n56\ttype symlinkMode int\n57\t\n58\tconst (\n59\t\tsymlinkP symlinkMode = iota\n60\t\tsymlinkH\n61\t\tsymlinkL\n62\t)\n63\t\n64\ttype options struct {\n65\t\treference     string\n66\t\trecursive     bool\n67\t\tnoDereference bool\n68\t\tsymlink       symlinkMode\n69\t}\n70\t\n71\tfunc main() {\n72\t\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n73\t\n74\t\topts, ownerSpec, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n75\t\tuid, gid := resolveOwnership(opts, ownerSpec)\n76\t\tif len(files) == 0 {\n77\t\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n78\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"chown: missing operand\")\n79\t\t\t} else {\n80\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: missing operand after '%s'\\n\", ownerSpec)\n81\t\t\t}\n82\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'chown --help' for more information.\")\n83\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n84\t\t}\n85\t\n86\t\texitCode := 0\n87\t\tfor _, file := range files {\n88\t\t\tif err := changeOwnership(opts, uid, gid, file); err != nil {\n89\t\t\t\texitCode = 1\n90\t\t\t}\n91\t\t}\n92\t\tif exitCode != 0 {\n93\t\t\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n94\t\t}\n95\t}\n96\t\n97\tfunc changeOwnership(opts options, uid, gid int, path string) error {\n98\t\tif !opts.recursive {\n99\t\t\treturn chownSingle(opts, uid, gid, path)\n100\t\t}\n101\t\treturn chownRecursive(opts, uid, gid, path, true)\n102\t}\n103\t\n104\tfunc chownSingle(opts options, uid, gid int, path string) error {\n105\t\tfn := os.Chown\n106\t\tif opts.noDereference {\n107\t\t\tfn = os.Lchown\n108\t\t}\n109\t\tif err := fn(path, uid, gid); err != nil {\n110\t\t\treportError(err)\n111\t\t\treturn err\n112\t\t}\n113\t\treturn nil\n114\t}\n115\t\n116\tfunc chownRecursive(opts options, uid, gid int, path string, isTopLevel bool) error {\n117\t\tfollow := shouldFollowLink(opts, isTopLevel)\n118\t\tfi, err := statPath(path, follow)\n119\t\tif err != nil {\n120\t\t\treportError(err)\n121\t\t\treturn err\n122\t\t}\n123\t\tvar firstErr error\n124\t\tif fi.IsDir() {\n125\t\t\tfirstErr = walkChildren(opts, uid, gid, path)\n126\t\t}\n127\t\tif err := applyChown(opts, uid, gid, path); err != nil && firstErr == nil {\n128\t\t\tfirstErr = err\n129\t\t}\n130\t\treturn firstErr\n131\t}\n132\t\n133\tfunc applyChown(opts options, uid, gid int, path string) error {\n134\t\tfn := os.Lchown\n135\t\tif opts.symlink == symlinkL {\n136\t\t\tfn = os.Chown\n137\t\t}\n138\t\tif err := fn(path, uid, gid); err != nil {\n139\t\t\treportError(err)\n140\t\t\treturn err\n141\t\t}\n142\t\treturn nil\n143\t}\n144\t\n145\tfunc shouldFollowLink(opts options, isTopLevel bool) bool {\n146\t\tswitch opts.symlink {\n147\t\tcase symlinkL:\n148\t\t\treturn true\n149\t\tcase symlinkH:\n150\t\t\treturn isTopLevel\n151\t\tdefault:\n152\t\t\treturn false\n153\t\t}\n154\t}\n155\t\n156\tfunc statPath(path string, follow bool) (os.FileInfo, error) {\n157\t\tif follow {\n158\t\t\treturn os.Stat(path)\n159\t\t}\n160\t\treturn os.Lstat(path)\n161\t}\n162\t\n163\tfunc walkChildren(opts options, uid, gid int, dir string) error {\n164\t\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dir)\n165\t\tif err != nil {\n166\t\t\treportError(err)\n167\t\t\treturn err\n168\t\t}\n169\t\tvar firstErr error\n170\t\tfor _, e := range entries {\n171\t\t\tchild := filepath.Join(dir, e.Name())\n172\t\t\tif err := chownRecursive(opts, uid, gid, child, false); err != nil && firstErr == nil {\n173\t\t\t\tfirstErr = err\n174\t\t\t}\n175\t\t}\n176\t\treturn firstErr\n177\t}\n178\t\n179\tfunc resolveOwnership(opts options, ownerSpec string) (int, int) {\n180\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n181\t\t\treturn resolveReference(opts.reference)\n182\t\t}\n183\t\treturn parseOwnerSpec(ownerSpec)\n184\t}\n185\t\n186\tfunc parseOwnerSpec(spec string) (int, int) {\n187\t\towner, group, hasColon := strings.Cut(spec, \":\")\n188\t\tif !hasColon {\n189\t\t\treturn lookupUser(spec), -1\n190\t\t}\n191\t\tuid := -1\n192\t\tif owner != \"\" {\n193\t\t\tuid = lookupUser(owner)\n194\t\t}\n195\t\tif group != \"\" {\n196\t\t\treturn uid, lookupGroup(group, spec)\n197\t\t}\n198\t\tif owner == \"\" {\n199\t\t\treturn -1, -1\n200\t\t}\n201\t\treturn uid, lookupLoginGroup(owner)\n202\t}\n203\t\n204\tfunc lookupUser(name string) int {\n205\t\tif uid, err := strconv.Atoi(name); err == nil {\n206\t\t\treturn uid\n207\t\t}\n208\t\tu, err := user.Lookup(name)\n209\t\tif err != nil {\n210\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", name)\n211\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n212\t\t}\n213\t\tuid, err := strconv.Atoi(u.Uid)\n214\t\tif err != nil {\n215\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", name)\n216\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n217\t\t}\n218\t\treturn uid\n219\t}\n220\t\n221\tfunc lookupGroup(name string, spec string) int {\n222\t\tif gid, err := strconv.Atoi(name); err == nil {\n223\t\t\treturn gid\n224\t\t}\n225\t\tg, err := user.LookupGroup(name)\n226\t\tif err != nil {\n227\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", spec)\n228\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n229\t\t}\n230\t\tgid, err := strconv.Atoi(g.Gid)\n231\t\tif err != nil {\n232\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", spec)\n233\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n234\t\t}\n235\t\treturn gid\n236\t}\n237\t\n238\tfunc lookupLoginGroup(owner string) int {\n239\t\tu, err := user.Lookup(owner)\n240\t\tif err != nil {\n241\t\t\tu, err = user.LookupId(owner)\n242\t\t\tif err != nil {\n243\t\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", owner)\n244\t\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n245\t\t\t}\n246\t\t}\n247\t\tgid, err := strconv.Atoi(u.Gid)\n248\t\tif err != nil {\n249\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", owner)\n250\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n251\t\t}\n252\t\treturn gid\n253\t}\n254\t\n255\tfunc resolveReference(rfile string) (int, int) {\n256\t\tfi, err := sys.Stat(rfile)\n257\t\tif err != nil {\n258\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: failed to get attributes of '%s': %s\\n\",\n259\t\t\t\trfile, err.(*os.PathError).Err)\n260\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n261\t\t}\n262\t\treturn int(fi.Uid), int(fi.Gid)\n263\t}\n264\t\n265\tfunc reportError(err error) {\n266\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n267\t}\n268\t\n269\tfunc formatErr(err error) string {\n270\t\tif pe, ok := errors.AsType[*os.PathError](err); ok {\n271\t\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"changing ownership of '%s': %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n272\t\t}\n273\t\treturn err.Error()\n274\t}\n275\t\n276\tfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, string, []string) {\n277\t\tvar opts options\n278\t\tvar files []string\n279\t\townerSpec := \"\"\n280\t\tendOfFlags := false\n281\t\tfor _, arg := range args {\n282\t\t\tif endOfFlags {\n283\t\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n284\t\t\t\tcontinue\n285\t\t\t}\n286\t\t\tif handled := handleSpecialArg(arg, &endOfFlags); handled {\n287\t\t\t\tcontinue\n288\t\t\t}\n289\t\t\tif parseLongFlag(arg, &opts) {\n290\t\t\t\tcontinue\n291\t\t\t}\n292\t\t\tif ownerSpec == \"\" {\n293\t\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1 && parseShortFlags(arg[1:], &opts) {\n294\t\t\t\t\tcontinue\n295\t\t\t\t}\n296\t\t\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n297\t\t\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n298\t\t\t\t} else {\n299\t\t\t\t\townerSpec = arg\n300\t\t\t\t}\n301\t\t\t} else {\n302\t\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n303\t\t\t}\n304\t\t}\n305\t\tif ownerSpec == \"\" && opts.reference == \"\" {\n306\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"chown: missing operand\")\n307\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'chown --help' for more information.\")\n308\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n309\t\t}\n310\t\treturn opts, ownerSpec, files\n311\t}\n312\t\n313\tfunc handleSpecialArg(arg string, endOfFlags *bool) bool {\n314\t\tswitch arg {\n315\t\tcase \"--help\":\n316\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n317\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n318\t\tcase \"--version\":\n319\t\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n320\t\t\tos.Exit(0)\n321\t\tcase \"--\":\n322\t\t\t*endOfFlags = true\n323\t\tdefault:\n324\t\t\treturn false\n325\t\t}\n326\t\treturn true\n327\t}\n328\t\n329\tfunc parseLongFlag(arg string, opts *options) bool {\n330\t\tswitch arg {\n331\t\tcase \"--verbose\", \"--changes\", \"--silent\", \"--quiet\":\n332\t\tcase \"--recursive\":\n333\t\t\topts.recursive = true\n334\t\tcase \"--dereference\":\n335\t\t\topts.noDereference = false\n336\t\tcase \"--no-dereference\":\n337\t\t\topts.noDereference = true\n338\t\tcase \"--preserve-root\", \"--no-preserve-root\":\n339\t\tdefault:\n340\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--reference=\") {\n341\t\t\t\topts.reference = arg[len(\"--reference=\"):]\n342\t\t\t\treturn true\n343\t\t\t}\n344\t\t\treturn false\n345\t\t}\n346\t\treturn true\n347\t}\n348\t\n349\tfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) bool {\n350\t\tfor _, c := range flags {\n351\t\t\tswitch c {\n352\t\t\tcase 'v', 'c', 'f':\n353\t\t\tcase 'R':\n354\t\t\t\topts.recursive = true\n355\t\t\tcase 'h':\n356\t\t\t\topts.noDereference = true\n357\t\t\tcase 'H':\n358\t\t\t\topts.symlink = symlinkH\n359\t\t\tcase 'L':\n360\t\t\t\topts.symlink = symlinkL\n361\t\t\tcase 'P':\n362\t\t\t\topts.symlink = symlinkP\n363\t\t\tdefault:\n364\t\t\t\treturn false\n365\t\t\t}\n366\t\t}\n367\t\treturn true\n368\t}\n369\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a39bb1de-8019-4cee-97a2-987b3a588d8f","uuid":"6ad3f03d-7d77-440a-b083-55ad9b6ce63a","timestamp":"2026-05-24T01:55:09.268Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/cmd/chown/main.go","content":"// Copyright (c) 2026 Petar Djukic. All rights reserved.\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\n\n// cmd/chown implements srd091-chown R1.1-R1.4, R2.1-R2.3.\npackage main\n\nimport (\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"os/user\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"strconv\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/petar-djukic/go-unix-utils/pkg/sys\"\n)\n\nconst helpText = `Usage: chown [OPTION]... [OWNER][:[GROUP]] FILE...\n  or:  chown [OPTION]... --reference=RFILE FILE...\nChange the owner and/or group of each FILE to OWNER and/or GROUP.\n\n  -c, --changes          like verbose but report only when a change is made\n  -f, --silent, --quiet  suppress most error messages\n  -v, --verbose          output a diagnostic for every file processed\n      --dereference      affect the referent of each symbolic link (this is\n                         the default), rather than the symbolic link itself\n  -h, --no-dereference   affect symbolic links instead of any referenced file\n      --no-preserve-root  do not treat '/' specially (the default)\n      --preserve-root    fail to operate recursively on '/'\n      --reference=RFILE  use RFILE's owner and group rather than specifying\n                         OWNER:GROUP values\n  -R, --recursive        operate on files and directories recursively\n  -H                     if a command line argument is a symbolic link\n                         to a directory, traverse it\n  -L                     traverse every symbolic link to a directory\n                         encountered\n  -P                     do not traverse any symbolic links (default)\n      --help     display this help and exit\n      --version  output version information and exit\n\nOwner is unchanged if missing.  Group is unchanged if missing, but changed\nto login group if implied by a ':' following a symbolic OWNER.\nOWNER and GROUP may be numeric as well as symbolic.\n\nExamples:\n  chown root /u        Change the owner of /u to \"root\".\n  chown root:staff /u  Change the owner of /u to \"root\" and the\n                       group to \"staff\".\n  chown -hR root /u    Change the owner of /u and subfiles to \"root\".\n`\n\nconst versionText = `chown (go-unix-utils) dev\n`\n\ntype symlinkMode int\n\nconst (\n\tsymlinkP symlinkMode = iota\n\tsymlinkH\n\tsymlinkL\n)\n\ntype options struct {\n\treference     string\n\trecursive     bool\n\tnoDereference bool\n\tsymlink       symlinkMode\n}\n\nfunc main() {\n\tsys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()\n\n\topts, ownerSpec, files := parseArgs(os.Args[1:])\n\tuid, gid := resolveOwnership(opts, ownerSpec)\n\tif len(files) == 0 {\n\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"chown: missing operand\")\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: missing operand after '%s'\\n\", ownerSpec)\n\t\t}\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'chown --help' for more information.\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\n\texitCode := 0\n\tfor _, file := range files {\n\t\tif err := changeOwnership(opts, uid, gid, file); err != nil {\n\t\t\texitCode = 1\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif exitCode != 0 {\n\t\tos.Exit(exitCode)\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc changeOwnership(opts options, uid, gid int, path string) error {\n\tif !opts.recursive {\n\t\treturn chownSingle(opts, uid, gid, path)\n\t}\n\treturn chownRecursive(opts, uid, gid, path, true)\n}\n\nfunc chownSingle(opts options, uid, gid int, path string) error {\n\tfn := os.Chown\n\tif opts.noDereference {\n\t\tfn = os.Lchown\n\t}\n\tif err := fn(path, uid, gid); err != nil {\n\t\treportError(err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc chownRecursive(opts options, uid, gid int, path string, isTopLevel bool) error {\n\tfollow := shouldFollowLink(opts, isTopLevel)\n\tfi, err := statPath(path, follow)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treportError(err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tvar firstErr error\n\tif fi.IsDir() {\n\t\tfirstErr = walkChildren(opts, uid, gid, path)\n\t}\n\tif err := applyChown(opts, uid, gid, path); err != nil && firstErr == nil {\n\t\tfirstErr = err\n\t}\n\treturn firstErr\n}\n\nfunc applyChown(opts options, uid, gid int, path string) error {\n\tfn := os.Lchown\n\tif opts.symlink == symlinkL {\n\t\tfn = os.Chown\n\t}\n\tif err := fn(path, uid, gid); err != nil {\n\t\treportError(err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\nfunc shouldFollowLink(opts options, isTopLevel bool) bool {\n\tswitch opts.symlink {\n\tcase symlinkL:\n\t\treturn true\n\tcase symlinkH:\n\t\treturn isTopLevel\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n}\n\nfunc statPath(path string, follow bool) (os.FileInfo, error) {\n\tif follow {\n\t\treturn os.Stat(path)\n\t}\n\treturn os.Lstat(path)\n}\n\nfunc walkChildren(opts options, uid, gid int, dir string) error {\n\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(dir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treportError(err)\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tvar firstErr error\n\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\tchild := filepath.Join(dir, e.Name())\n\t\tif err := chownRecursive(opts, uid, gid, child, false); err != nil && firstErr == nil {\n\t\t\tfirstErr = err\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn firstErr\n}\n\nfunc resolveOwnership(opts options, ownerSpec string) (int, int) {\n\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n\t\treturn resolveReference(opts.reference)\n\t}\n\treturn parseOwnerSpec(ownerSpec)\n}\n\nfunc parseOwnerSpec(spec string) (int, int) {\n\towner, group, hasColon := strings.Cut(spec, \":\")\n\tif !hasColon {\n\t\treturn lookupUser(spec), -1\n\t}\n\tuid := -1\n\tif owner != \"\" {\n\t\tuid = lookupUser(owner)\n\t}\n\tif group != \"\" {\n\t\treturn uid, lookupGroup(group, spec)\n\t}\n\tif owner == \"\" {\n\t\treturn -1, -1\n\t}\n\treturn uid, lookupLoginGroup(owner)\n}\n\nfunc lookupUser(name string) int {\n\tif uid, err := strconv.Atoi(name); err == nil {\n\t\treturn uid\n\t}\n\tu, err := user.Lookup(name)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", name)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\tuid, err := strconv.Atoi(u.Uid)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", name)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn uid\n}\n\nfunc lookupGroup(name string, spec string) int {\n\tif gid, err := strconv.Atoi(name); err == nil {\n\t\treturn gid\n\t}\n\tg, err := user.LookupGroup(name)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", spec)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\tgid, err := strconv.Atoi(g.Gid)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid group: '%s'\\n\", spec)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn gid\n}\n\nfunc lookupLoginGroup(owner string) int {\n\tu, err := user.Lookup(owner)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tu, err = user.LookupId(owner)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", owner)\n\t\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tgid, err := strconv.Atoi(u.Gid)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: invalid user: '%s'\\n\", owner)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn gid\n}\n\nfunc resolveReference(rfile string) (int, int) {\n\tfi, err := sys.Stat(rfile)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: failed to get attributes of '%s': %s\\n\",\n\t\t\trfile, err.(*os.PathError).Err)\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn int(fi.Uid), int(fi.Gid)\n}\n\nfunc reportError(err error) {\n\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"chown: %s\\n\", formatErr(err))\n}\n\nfunc formatErr(err error) string {\n\tif pe, ok := errors.AsType[*os.PathError](err); ok {\n\t\treturn fmt.Sprintf(\"changing ownership of '%s': %s\", pe.Path, pe.Err)\n\t}\n\treturn err.Error()\n}\n\nfunc parseArgs(args []string) (options, string, []string) {\n\tvar opts options\n\tvar files []string\n\townerSpec := \"\"\n\tendOfFlags := false\n\tfor _, arg := range args {\n\t\tif endOfFlags {\n\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif handled := handleSpecialArg(arg, &endOfFlags); handled {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif parseLongFlag(arg, &opts) {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif ownerSpec == \"\" {\n\t\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"-\") && len(arg) > 1 && parseShortFlags(arg[1:], &opts) {\n\t\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif opts.reference != \"\" {\n\t\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n\t\t\t} else {\n\t\t\t\townerSpec = arg\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t} else {\n\t\t\tfiles = append(files, arg)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\tif ownerSpec == \"\" && opts.reference == \"\" {\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"chown: missing operand\")\n\t\tfmt.Fprintln(os.Stderr, \"Try 'chown --help' for more information.\")\n\t\tos.Exit(1)\n\t}\n\treturn opts, ownerSpec, files\n}\n\nfunc handleSpecialArg(arg string, endOfFlags *bool) bool {\n\tswitch arg {\n\tcase \"--help\":\n\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, helpText)\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\tcase \"--version\":\n\t\tfmt.Fprint(os.Stdout, versionText)\n\t\tos.Exit(0)\n\tcase \"--\":\n\t\t*endOfFlags = true\n\tdefault:\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc parseLongFlag(arg string, opts *options) bool {\n\tswitch arg {\n\tcase \"--verbose\", \"--changes\", \"--silent\", \"--quiet\":\n\tcase \"--recursive\":\n\t\topts.recursive = true\n\tcase \"--dereference\":\n\t\topts.noDereference = false\n\tcase \"--no-dereference\":\n\t\topts.noDereference = true\n\tcase \"--preserve-root\", \"--no-preserve-root\":\n\tdefault:\n\t\tif strings.HasPrefix(arg, \"--reference=\") {\n\t\t\topts.reference = arg[len(\"--reference=\"):]\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn false\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\nfunc parseShortFlags(flags string, opts *options) bool {\n\tfor _, c := range flags {\n\t\tswitch c {\n\t\tcase 'v', 'c', 'f':\n\t\tcase 'R':\n\t\t\topts.recursive = true\n\t\tcase 'h':\n\t\t\topts.noDereference = true\n\t\tcase 'H':\n\t\t\topts.symlink = symlinkH\n\t\tcase 'L':\n\t\t\topts.symlink = symlinkL\n\t\tcase 'P':\n\t\t\topts.symlink = symlinkP\n\t\tdefault:\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n","numLines":369,"startLine":1,"totalLines":369}}}
