{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FzvTKcsJuN2FmQa1om5ho","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create a comprehensive summary of my findings:\n\n## Summary\n\nBased on my analysis of the codebase, here's what I found:\n\n### 1. **sys.Stat Return Type and Fields**\n\nThe `sys.Stat()` function returns a pointer to `FileInfo` struct defined at `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/pkg/sys/fileinfo.go`:\n\n```go\ntype FileInfo struct {\n    Mode       os.FileMode\n    Size       int64\n    Nlink      uint64\n    Uid        uint32      // <-- User ID field\n    Gid        uint32      // <-- Group ID field\n    Rdev       uint64\n    Dev        uint64\n    Ino        uint64\n    Blocks     int64\n    Blksize    int64\n    ModTime    time.Time\n    AccessTime time.Time\n    ChangeTime time.Time\n    Info       os.FileInfo\n}\n```\n\nThe key fields you need are **`Uid` (uint32)** and **`Gid` (uint32)** for user and group IDs respectively.\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Existing Verbose Output Implementations**\n\nI found three excellent reference implementations with verbose/changes output patterns:\n\n#### **cmd/chgrp/main.go** (Best Reference - Most Comprehensive)\nLocated at: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/cmd/chgrp/main.go`\n\nKey implementation details:\n- **Options struct** includes both `verbose` and `changes` flags\n- **`printDiagnostic()` function** (lines 242-260) handles the output logic:\n  - Returns early if neither verbose nor changes is set\n  - Checks if operation actually changed anything (`oldGID == newGID`)\n  - Verbose mode: prints every file including \"retained as\" messages\n  - Changes mode: only prints when actual change occurred\n  - Uses helper `gidToName()` to convert numeric GID to group name\n  - Format: `\"changed group of '%s' from %s to %s\\n\"` (path, old_name, new_name)\n\n#### **cmd/chmod/main.go** (Detailed Mode Formatting)\nLocated at: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/cmd/chmod/main.go`\n\nKey implementation details:\n- **`printDiagnostic()` function** (lines 142-152):\n  - Verbose mode: always prints\n  - Changes mode: only prints if `oldMode != newMode`\n  - Format includes both octal AND symbolic notation:\n    ```\n    \"mode of '%s' changed from %04o (%s) to %04o (%s)\\n\"\n    ```\n  - Uses `symbolicString()` to convert modes to rwxrwxrwx format\n\n#### **cmd/cp/main.go** (Simpler Verbose Pattern)\nLocated at: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/cmd/cp/main.go`\n\n- Uses a simple boolean `verbose` flag (lines 46, 144, 176-177)\n- Integrated throughout the copy logic to print progress\n\n#### **cmd/chown/main.go** (Verbose Parsing Only)\nLocated at: `/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5558/cmd/chown/main.go`\n\nNote: This command parses verbose/changes flags (line 331-332) but does **not** implement the printing logic yet - verbose output is currently a no-op. This might be intentional or a feature still to be implemented.\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Recommended Verbose Output Pattern for Your Command**\n\nBased on the chgrp/chmod implementations, here's the recommended pattern:\n\n1. **Add to options struct**: `verbose` and `changes` boolean flags\n2. **Create `printDiagnostic()` function** that:\n   - Checks both flags early (return if neither set)\n   - Calls stat before and after to get old vs. new values\n   - For verbose mode: always print\n   - For changes mode: only print if actual change occurred\n   - Uses ID-to-name conversion for human-readable output\n3. **Message format**: Follow the chgrp pattern: `\"changed X of '%s' from Y to Z\\n\"`"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a39bb1de-8019-4cee-97a2-987b3a588d8f","uuid":"aefa391f-c50a-4b27-a064-36e1d0923517","times