{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01LPGtvdZZm8mFVcefSToXTB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is clear. When only group is being changed (`:group`), GNU chown uses `:groupname` format in the \"to\" part instead of `user:groupname`. My code shows `pdiddy:everyone` but GNU shows `:everyone`.\n\nThis means GNU chown preserves the format of what was specified. When you specify `:GROUP`, the verbose \"to\" shows `:GROUP`. When you specify `OWNER:GROUP`, it shows `OWNER:GROUP`. When you specify `OWNER`, it shows just `OWNER`.\n\nSo the \"to\" label should reflect the ownership spec format, not the resolved full ownership. \n\nI need to track what format was actually specified. Looking at the outputs, when the uid isn't being changed (uid is -1), the \"to\" should display `:group` instead of `user:group`, and when the gid isn't being changed, it should show just `user`. The \"from\" part always shows the full `user:group` format. The fix needs to be in how I format the ownership string based on what was actually specified versus what was resolved. Fixing the diagnostic output...\n\nThe key insight is that `formatOwnership` needs to see the actual target values (which might be -1) for the \"to\" label, but I still need the effective values for comparing what actually changed. So I'll call `formatOwnership(targetUID, targetGID)` directly for the label instead of using the computed effective values, while keeping the effective values for the comparison logic. Finishing the output message for when ownership is retained, then handling the final case where ownership actually changes—using the target values in the output so that -1 values display as just the group name rather than the full user:group format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2458,"cache_read_input_tokens":66701,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2458},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a39bb1de-8019-4cee-97a2-987b3a588d8f","uuid":"68193862-c008-4682-8305-79f6ceb87dfe"}
